The '''2024 FIFA Intercontinental Cup final''', also known simply as the '''2024 FIFA Intercontinental Cup''',<ref name="key info">{{cite news |date=20 September 2024 |title=FIFA Intercontinental Cup: Key information|url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/intercontinentalcup/2024/articles/information-tournament-details|work=[[FIFA]]|access-date=20 September 2024}}</ref> was the final match of the [[2024 FIFA Intercontinental Cup]], an international club [[association football|football]] tournament. It was the first final of the [[FIFA Intercontinental Cup]], a [[FIFA]]-organised tournament between the club champions from each of the six continental confederations.<ref name="Reuters-new cup">{{cite news |last=Nair |first=Rohith |date=17 December 2023 |title=Club World Cup set for June-July 2025, new Intercontinental Cup in 2024 –FIFA |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/club-world-cup-set-june-july-2025-new-intercontinental-cup-2024-fifa-2023-12-17/ |agency=[[Reuters]] |archive-url=https://archive.today/20240206181157/https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/club-world-cup-set-june-july-2025-new-intercontinental-cup-2024-fifa-2023-12-17/ |archive-date=6 February 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

The match took place at [[Lusail Stadium]] in [[Lusail]], Qatar, on 18 December 2024 between Spanish club [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]], the winners of the [[2023–24 UEFA Champions League]], and Mexican club [[C.F. Pachuca|Pachuca]], the winners of play-offs contested by the other five confederations.<ref>{{cite web |last=Bonn |first=Kyle |date=17 December 2023 |title=Club World Cup 2025 in USA: Confirmed teams, format, schedule, dates for FIFA tournament with expanded field |url=https://www.sportingnews.com/us/soccer/news/club-world-cup-2025-usa-teams-format-dates-schedule-fifa/d5370f31621951fc1e4499e7 |work=[[The Sporting News]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240123204627/https://www.sportingnews.com/us/soccer/news/club-world-cup-2025-usa-teams-format-dates-schedule-fifa/d5370f31621951fc1e4499e7 |archive-date=23 January 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Real Madrid won the match 3–0 to win the inaugural FIFA Intercontinental Cup, which was also its sixth FIFA trophy and ninth [[List of world champion football clubs|club world championship]] title.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/fifa-club-world-cup/articles/real-madrid-pachuca-report-final |title=Real Madrid beat Pachuca to win Intercontinental Cup |publisher=[[FIFA]] |date=18 December 2024 |access-date=18 December 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c205nv1yr6pt|title=Real Madrid 3 Pachuca 0|date=18 December 2024|work=BBC Sport|accessdate=19 December 2024}}</ref>

